Quest System

Purpose

The quest system provides a structured path through the progression of the pack.

Quests should guide the player through technological development without replacing exploration, experimentation, or the GuideME handbook.

The quest system should explain what the player can do next, why it matters, and what systems are being introduced.

Quests should follow the progression defined by the Progression documents.

Quest Structure

The quest system should be divided into progression chapters.

Each chapter represents a major stage of technological development.

Chapters should generally follow:

Starting Point

Primitive Age

Steam Age

LV

MV

HV

EV

IV

LuV

ZPM

UV

UHV

Post-Endgame

Additional chapters may exist for systems that require independent progression, such as Magic, Apotheosis, ProjectE, and Avaritia.

Starting Point Chapter

The Starting Point chapter introduces the player to the basic survival progression.

It should cover:

Basic survival

Basic tools

Basic resources

Basic shelter

Early exploration

Initial resource gathering

The chapter should eventually direct the player toward technological progression.

Primitive Age Chapter

The Primitive Age chapter introduces the first technological systems.

It should explain:

Primitive industrial materials

Basic processing

Primitive machines

Early automation

Initial industrial infrastructure

The final quests should lead toward the Steam Age.

Steam Age Chapter

The Steam Age introduces the first major industrial systems.

It should cover:

Steam power

Create mechanical systems

Early GregTech progression

Modern Industrialization systems

Mechanical automation

Early industrial infrastructure

The chapter should establish the foundation for electrical technology.

Electrical Chapters

LV, MV, HV, EV, IV, LuV, ZPM, UV, and UHV should each have their own progression chapter.

Each chapter should introduce:

New materials

New machines

New processing chains

New power requirements

New automation capabilities

New cross-mod interactions

The chapter should explain what changed from the previous tier and what infrastructure is required to advance.

Quest Dependencies

Important quests should have meaningful prerequisites.

A quest may require:

A previous quest

A specific machine

A specific material

A specific technological tier

A completed processing chain

A required power infrastructure

A cross-mod component

A required automated production system

Quest dependencies should reflect the actual progression.

Quests should not suggest that the player can access systems that are still progression-gated.

Quest Objectives

Quest objectives should focus on meaningful progression milestones.

Examples include:

Obtaining an important material

Crafting a major machine

Building a new power system

Completing a processing chain

Automating an important resource

Establishing a factory

Unlocking a new technological tier

Completing a major cross-mod integration

Objectives should avoid excessive busywork.

The purpose of a quest is to communicate progression rather than force the player to repeatedly perform trivial actions.

Quest Rewards

Rewards should support progression without invalidating it.

Possible rewards include:

Small quantities of useful materials

Basic resources

Exploration supplies

Documentation

Cosmetic rewards

Useful early-game equipment

Limited progression support items

Rewards should never provide major progression materials significantly earlier than intended.

High-tier rewards should be carefully controlled.

Cross-Mod Quests

Important cross-mod interactions should be represented by quests.

Examples include:

Using Create to support industrial logistics

Using Mekanism for chemical processing

Using Modern Industrialization for complementary processing

Using AE2 for automated logistics

Using Create Aeronautics for advanced transportation

Using Create Big Cannons for advanced industrial weaponry

Cross-mod quests should encourage the player to understand why different systems exist.

Automation Quests

Automation should become increasingly important as progression advances.

Early quests may introduce simple automation.

Later quests should encourage:

Continuous production

Parallel production

Automated processing

Automated resource generation

Digital logistics

Large-scale factory infrastructure

Endgame automation

Automation should be presented as the intended solution to increasing production requirements.

Magic Chapter

Magic should have its own progression chapter.

The magic progression should not simply be inserted into the technological chapters.

Magic quests should introduce:

Magical resources

Magic systems

Rituals

Magical machines

Exploration

Magical progression tiers

Cross-mod interactions

Magic should remain a distinct progression path while interacting with the technological progression where appropriate.

Apotheosis Chapter

Apotheosis should receive dedicated progression quests.

The chapter should introduce:

Apotheosis systems

Enchanting progression

Affix progression

Boss progression

Advanced equipment

Late-game Apotheosis systems

Apotheosis progression should remain gated by the main progression.

ProjectE Chapter

ProjectE should be treated as post-endgame content.

Its quests should introduce:

ProjectE systems

The ProjectE unlock requirement

The Ultimate Transmutation Core

EMC progression

Advanced transmutation

Energy Condensers

Post-endgame automation

The final ProjectE milestone

ProjectE should not be available during normal technological progression.

Avaritia Chapter

Avaritia should represent one of the final progression systems.

Its quests should introduce:

Avaritia systems

Extreme Crafting

Neutronium progression

Infinity progression

Extreme components

Final crafting goals

Avaritia should require substantial completion of the main progression.

Post-Endgame Chapter

The Post-Endgame chapter should contain the largest and most demanding objectives in the quest system.

It should cover:

Extreme automation

Cross-mod production

Massive resource requirements

Advanced AE2 infrastructure

ProjectE

Avaritia

Advanced exploration

Magic endgame

Large-scale industrial infrastructure

Final progression milestones

The final quests should require mastery of multiple systems rather than completion of a single mod.

Quest Completion

Completing a chapter should represent meaningful progression.

Chapter completion may unlock:

New quests

New systems

New recipes

New documentation

New progression stages

New endgame objectives

Quest completion should never be the only mechanism enforcing progression.

Recipes, machines, materials, and technological gates must remain independently enforced.

GuideME Integration

The quest system and GuideME handbook should complement each other.

Quests should provide direction and objectives.

GuideME should provide detailed explanations and reference information.

GuideME should document:

Technological systems

Materials

Machines

Processing chains

Power systems

Cross-mod interactions

Progression rules

Advanced systems

Players should be able to use the quest system to know what to do and GuideME to understand how the systems work.

Final Goal

The quest system should make the progression understandable without making it linear or restrictive.

Players should know what technological milestone they are working toward while still being able to explore, build factories, experiment with automation, and develop their own infrastructure.

The quest system should document the journey through the pack rather than replace the journey itself.
